 "styleRules": [
  "Faceted realism (docs/design/ArtStyle.md style A): real hand and forearm proportions built from chunky flat-shaded facets, like a carved figure. Skin rings have FIXED face directions, so every band between two rings is a flat facet (no twisted quads crumpling into small triangles); the palm and the thenar-and-web wedge are convex hulls (every face one plane). 6-sided fingers and thumb with one band per phalanx, a 12-sided palm block (three-plane back and palm, bevelled sides), 10-sided sleeves; no nails or wrinkles.",
  "One skin per hand: palm, thenar-and-web wedge, thumb and fingers (and the hidden core of the fist) are unioned into one closed mesh (exact boolean), so the parts meet in clean crease lines with no shell intersections.",
  "Painted, not textured: one flat value per modelled facet (+-3.5% per phalanx or panel, +-3% per facet, slight warm/cool drift; all triangles of a face share it), warmer knuckles and fingertips, lighter palms; two-radius AO multiplied in (never below half the painted value; warm on the skin); a 0.0085-0.013-stud bevel normal only rounds the facet edges.",
  "Matte: roughness 0.80-0.86 skin, 0.92-0.95 sleeve; metalness 0.",
  "Tintable: both ColorMaps are neutral light bases. SurfaceAppearance.Color multiplies them: the avatar's arm colour on the Skin parts, any colour on the Sleeve parts (default charcoal)."
 ],
